git commit -m "ADR-102: the harness had never touched the camera" -m "ADR-101 reported 1966 controls checked against a stated expectation. A deep audit of what a user can actually ENTER was run against that claim and found four surfaces no harness had ever touched: twelve checkboxes that no kind s selector matched, one time field that the text kind s three types did not include, five file inputs that were excluded on purpose, and three drop zones that no CSS selector can find at all." -m "The file exclusion is the one worth naming plainly. ADR-101 wrote that a file chooser needs OS focus and an approval policy the gateway does not own. That confused the native DIALOG with the act of handing a page some bytes. The dialog is still out of scope and still never opens; the bytes were always ours to supply. Behind that confusion sat the kit s only photo entry - accept=image/* multiple on stand-sheet, never once driven - and the camera button in front of it was being reported as an Add that added no row." -m "Photo entry is wired three ways. Real bytes, made in the harness rather than read from disk: eight fixture files - a JPEG, a PNG, a WebM, a JSON pack, an .eco session, a CSV and a deliberately corrupt file - so a run reads nothing of the operator s disk and needs no fixture directory. One of them is called DJI_0192.JPG, because a page that keys on a filename should be driven with a filename somebody will really hand it. Hidden inputs are driven, because three of the five file inputs in this kit are display:none by design with a camera or Load-pack button standing in front of them, and a user reaches them. And drop zones are found by wrapping addEventListener and stamping the element as the drop listener registers, because a drop listener leaves no mark in the markup." -m "Measured: stand-sheet s file input verified, naming both IMG_0431.jpg and DJI_0192.JPG on the page; its drop zone verified, naming the photo it was dropped; and the camera button verified against what it actually does, because opening the chooser IS its result - HTMLInputElement.click is wrapped so the native dialog never opens and the request is counted instead. One of ADR-101 s eighteen findings retires as a false positive." -m "And a real defect, read against the source. stand-sheet s photo drop zone discards anything that is not an image in silence: the filter returns early on a non-image, and the only message the page ever gives is gated on whether anything was added. Drop a folder with a video in it, or the drone s flight log beside its frames, and the frames appear and the rest is gone without a word. Under this harness s own rule, a control that declines has to say so." -m "On video: no page in this kit accepts one or records one - the word appears only in the teachers guide, describing scoring behaviour from a recording made elsewhere. Rather than invent a surface, the harness carries a .webm fixture so that a page which SHOULD refuse one can be shown refusing it, which is how the silent discard above was found. What the harness does record is itself: every page run is filmed at 390x844 and a still is taken in the state each finding was reported in. A film is kept only where there is something to watch - 17 of 40 pages this run - because forty films of a page behaving is forty films nobody opens." -m "tools/probe.py adds three passes whose shape is different from the swarm s: no per-control expectation, only invariants - is this still a page, and did it say something when it refused. EDGES drives every field with every value that has ever broken a form: empty, whitespace, zero, negative, enormous, 1e308, a decimal where an integer belongs, letters in a number, an impossible date, four hundred characters, emoji, markup, and the separators an export has to quote. CHAOS takes N random actions from whatever is on screen with a seed, checking the invariants after every single one, and when one breaks the finding carries the seed and the exact list of actions so the sequence REPLAYS instead of being retold. EXPLORE walks every path through a key, depth-first to a leaf and then reload-and-replay to take the next branch - reload rather than undo, because a page has no obligation to be reversible and a walk that assumes it is will quietly explore a tree that is not there." -m "The passes: 344 fields times 14 values is 4284 entries, 16 findings. 2786 random actions, 151 findings. 859 paths, 413 leaves, 657 options, 276 distinct states, deepest 14, and no findings - the keys are sound." -m "What they found. field-season throws 26 uncaught TypeErrors under random pressing and ordination throws twice. farm-scout loses 76 percent of its rendered text after a particular sequence - the page is still there and most of it is not. ecology-lab renders NaN to infinity in a readout on an edge value, and NaN in its Hardy-Weinberg block. tree-proofs renders NaN under random pressing. And a four-hundred-character entry breaks the layout of eight pages, pushing content 3400 to 3700 pixels sideways on a 390 pixel phone." -m "That last one closes a loop. ADR-100 found a rule that can never fire: .row2 .g span declaring text-overflow ellipsis with no white-space nowrap, copied into fifteen pages. This is what it was supposed to prevent. Ethogram s div.row2 measured 3092 pixels wide under chaos, and div.g - the very element whose text was meant to be truncated - measured 3010. A dead rule was filed as a tidiness defect. It should have been filed as the reason a species name too long for a phone takes the page with it." -m "Six defects, all of them the instrument s. The battery was testing a tenth of the fields, because edges and chaos filtered candidates on the visibility recorded in the snapshot taken at load and most fields in this kit live in a pane that is shut - breeding-bench went from 3 fields and 42 values to 14 fields and 196. A time field was handed a text sentinel, which the browser discards before the page ever sees it, and deployment-log s start time was reported as throwing an entry away. A decline was counted in only one voice: ethogram explains a bad pack through alert, and the harness counting only toasts reported it as taking a file and saying nothing. The word undefined in a sentence was read as a value leaking, when ecology-lab writes R equals 0, the estimate is undefined, as a careful sentence - NaN and object Object are never English and still count anywhere, while undefined and null now count only where a value belongs. explore could not back up, because it reloaded by asking the plugin to open the page by kit name, which no fixture has; a reload action was published, since backtracking must not depend on a client knowing where the page came from. And the excluded list had grown a fourth member with a wrong reason." -m "Showing it fail. verify_probe writes five fixtures and asserts each pass both ways: a readout that goes NaN on a letter is reported and a guarded one is not; a page that breaks on the third press is found by random pressing and the finding carries the seed and the exact actions; the same seed twice gives the same run; a sound page reports nothing. The tree fixture is a real binary key - 14 nodes, 8 leaves, every node its own control - and the assertion is not that the walk went in but that it saw all fourteen, reached depth 3, and touched more distinct states than the key has leaves. Explored the key is a counting claim, so it is asserted as one. A NaN leaf three levels down is found, with the path taken to reach it and a picture of it. verify_swarm gains a photo fixture, a page that takes the photo and never says so, and a checkbox that will not stay ticked." -m "Numbers: 3571 affordances discovered, 1975 verified against an expectation, 17 wrong, 273 changed with no expectation stated, 32 that left no trace, 220 never visible, 3 the harness could not drive, 1051 excluded each with a reason, 15474 commands. Suite 64 of 64 jobs green, 4457 of 4457 checks passing, up from 63 and 4415; verify_swarm 40/40 was 28, verify_probe 25/25 new, verify_contract 70/70 was 65. No page changed and nothing was republished." -m "Not done: the export and re-import round trip, which is the strongest question to ask a pack importer - export, re-import, compare - and which attach-file cannot ask because it takes fixture names only. Hidden is 220 rather than ADR-101 s 204 because the surface widened; ten of experiment-guide s checkboxes sit in a pane no tab opens." -m "Next, and falsifiable. field-season throws twenty-six times under random pressing and ordination twice, and I claim these are the same defect: a handler reading a selection that chaos has cleared. I expect that to be wrong - that they are two unrelated null reads, and that at least one of them also fires on an ordinary path a user would take rather than only under random pressing. Falsifier: replaying both seeds, reading the two handlers, and finding a single shared cause that only a random order can reach. The replay is already in the ledger; the reading is the next slice."
